From be5470dfe34495996accbefe3511c4393a8f1b04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:14:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Program per-VLAN spanning tree into the kernel

mstpd computes the port states of every MSTI, but only passes the CIST
states to the kernel, so all VLANs follow the CIST.

Since Linux 5.18 the bridge supports per-VLAN spanning tree (bridge option
mst_enable): each VLAN is mapped to an MSTI, and each port has a state per
MSTI. switchdev drivers offload both.

On bridges with mst_enable, program the VLAN-to-MSTI mapping from the
VID-to-FID and FID-to-MSTID tables, and set the port states of the MSTIs.
The kernel only has a port state in an MSTI while the port is a member of
a VLAN of that MSTI, and a VLAN added later starts out with the CIST state.
So reprogram mapping and states whenever the kernel reports a VLAN change
(RTNLGRP_BRVLAN), and set only states the kernel reports. When a bridge is
removed from mstpd, map its VLANs back to the CIST.

The kernel cannot flush the forwarding database of a single MSTI; flush the
whole port instead.

Bridges without mst_enable behave as before.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
